[{:db/id 17592186087762 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43480c80-f56c-525c-8e3a-4535ddf6aa7b" "question-d43f6aa4-a331-53b3-b9d7-aed1378d0872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087584 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where\n![](images/fa/facc0c74a881851fc58355c5bf85ebb1e073d543a6c5e708e025ebbd61c69043.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n![](images/98/9839b4e4af6ba3ee215318c0a9b69844f33c0eea9bf426eb11701e60f3be91b3.svg)\n\nNotice that\n![](images/26/2697e4b0883667c64a7f1c24c370c6fb1f2e0b02c1c97d146cd9d5d9be17d963.svg)\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](images/5c/5cb3e4da19858e479f72aa783381f97e846d820117c141681d5791b09490f8e8.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087753 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087569 :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d5b37b3da99f0b93625ab8fd6ea72615da3159a8360fe267c3ae4a470fdd7af.svg)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector ![](images/01/01841df44c0029de31dd06a446211abb0bc0f6852d7bc76797204ae1d9a71e6c.svg) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](images/74/74c14f8d5615c146713a3c8ed31368a9843ed06f91d88a8745adf41764f8a003.svg)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087754 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-132fd44c-38e5-5ebe-8c05-231eab1b1859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087570 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](images/46/46bb3e9777a3944eb6b2f458911571442f57a5fae2f7aed1bb924522c51cad4a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-43480c80-f56c-525c-8e3a-4535ddf6aa7b" :question/id #uuid "43480c80-f56c-525c-8e3a-4535ddf6aa7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8028" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+(-1)y+1z \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+(-1)z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c212f72a-279f-54ef-b120-28592cf65c59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c212f72a-279f-54ef-b120-28592cf65c59" :answer-field/id #uuid "c212f72a-279f-54ef-b120-28592cf65c59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2cd1aa7-af9a-53f0-85ea-5b710aa150d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c79ee30-af5f-5bcf-8919-2afd0111f993" "answer-e56ff332-5e02-5683-904b-61aded3e9a3d" "answer-848ef172-7da8-5389-b025-51826e69cb7f" "answer-b2cd1aa7-af9a-53f0-85ea-5b710aa150d1" "answer-942631c7-0b88-56df-bbb6-0d0f79c6bd86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c79ee30-af5f-5bcf-8919-2afd0111f993" :answer/id #uuid "3c79ee30-af5f-5bcf-8919-2afd0111f993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e56ff332-5e02-5683-904b-61aded3e9a3d" :answer/id #uuid "e56ff332-5e02-5683-904b-61aded3e9a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-848ef172-7da8-5389-b025-51826e69cb7f" :answer/id #uuid "848ef172-7da8-5389-b025-51826e69cb7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2cd1aa7-af9a-53f0-85ea-5b710aa150d1" :answer/id #uuid "b2cd1aa7-af9a-53f0-85ea-5b710aa150d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-942631c7-0b88-56df-bbb6-0d0f79c6bd86" :answer/id #uuid "942631c7-0b88-56df-bbb6-0d0f79c6bd86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d43f6aa4-a331-53b3-b9d7-aed1378d0872" :question/id #uuid "d43f6aa4-a331-53b3-b9d7-aed1378d0872" :question/math-academy-id "q-140366" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{4},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $4\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-4)x+5y+(-1)z \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+7z \\\\ (-6)x+1y+0z \\\\ (-3)x+8y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-195d08c6-5530-555c-af06-ff33fffc4ac3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-195d08c6-5530-555c-af06-ff33fffc4ac3" :answer-field/id #uuid "195d08c6-5530-555c-af06-ff33fffc4ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-628defca-3da6-558b-ae06-2b8a5c25cb83" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2966ef61-eca9-5559-a74b-278b39bfedaf" "answer-fbc2ebcb-2249-5acb-9a0f-fbb1e11bec20" "answer-a0bb2cb9-6ad1-55c0-a805-436c0d8fe895" "answer-628defca-3da6-558b-ae06-2b8a5c25cb83" "answer-c19c982f-5333-5821-8069-e8c510e12f7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2966ef61-eca9-5559-a74b-278b39bfedaf" :answer/id #uuid "2966ef61-eca9-5559-a74b-278b39bfedaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 10 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbc2ebcb-2249-5acb-9a0f-fbb1e11bec20" :answer/id #uuid "fbc2ebcb-2249-5acb-9a0f-fbb1e11bec20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0bb2cb9-6ad1-55c0-a805-436c0d8fe895" :answer/id #uuid "a0bb2cb9-6ad1-55c0-a805-436c0d8fe895" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-628defca-3da6-558b-ae06-2b8a5c25cb83" :answer/id #uuid "628defca-3da6-558b-ae06-2b8a5c25cb83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c19c982f-5333-5821-8069-e8c510e12f7a" :answer/id #uuid "c19c982f-5333-5821-8069-e8c510e12f7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523" :question/id #uuid "93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523" :question/math-academy-id "q-96976" :question/problem "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+ax \\\\ bx+4y \\\\ cy+3x\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+3y \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ 3x-y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ -y+3x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ (-2)x+4y \\\\ (-1)y+3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=5+(-2)+(-1)=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-927c6a5b-b400-51f5-ba26-11160c313dcf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-927c6a5b-b400-51f5-ba26-11160c313dcf" :answer-field/id #uuid "927c6a5b-b400-51f5-ba26-11160c313dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002c537419e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4df16430-0c5c-51d3-b20c-0818ccaee58e" "answer-8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002c537419e7" "answer-3fb5a88e-2c16-50c0-a11b-1857fef41b83" "answer-d4787125-f5f3-5522-b754-798f786e8b21" "answer-89fb8e93-7da5-59dc-a467-6a051fba4e92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4df16430-0c5c-51d3-b20c-0818ccaee58e" :answer/id #uuid "4df16430-0c5c-51d3-b20c-0818ccaee58e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002c537419e7" :answer/id #uuid "8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002c537419e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fb5a88e-2c16-50c0-a11b-1857fef41b83" :answer/id #uuid "3fb5a88e-2c16-50c0-a11b-1857fef41b83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4787125-f5f3-5522-b754-798f786e8b21" :answer/id #uuid "d4787125-f5f3-5522-b754-798f786e8b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89fb8e93-7da5-59dc-a467-6a051fba4e92" :answer/id #uuid "89fb8e93-7da5-59dc-a467-6a051fba4e92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-132fd44c-38e5-5ebe-8c05-231eab1b1859" :question/id #uuid "132fd44c-38e5-5ebe-8c05-231eab1b1859" :question/math-academy-id "q-97031" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ff4e5fc-cb78-5911-9648-ab76b3946bbb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ff4e5fc-cb78-5911-9648-ab76b3946bbb" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ff4e5fc-cb78-5911-9648-ab76b3946bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e3fc592-6115-55a4-af5d-3458bd239697" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4be85799-67c5-5191-9977-b583cddea1c0" "answer-3e3fc592-6115-55a4-af5d-3458bd239697" "answer-0dde21cb-d15c-5e2a-8f75-04c7a50e62ec" "answer-684703ee-abb2-545a-9b7e-ac869bc848c7" "answer-f7a96820-7df4-5ed3-a1d2-40358ae6c6d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4be85799-67c5-5191-9977-b583cddea1c0" :answer/id #uuid "4be85799-67c5-5191-9977-b583cddea1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 28 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e3fc592-6115-55a4-af5d-3458bd239697" :answer/id #uuid "3e3fc592-6115-55a4-af5d-3458bd239697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dde21cb-d15c-5e2a-8f75-04c7a50e62ec" :answer/id #uuid "0dde21cb-d15c-5e2a-8f75-04c7a50e62ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 28 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-684703ee-abb2-545a-9b7e-ac869bc848c7" :answer/id #uuid "684703ee-abb2-545a-9b7e-ac869bc848c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7a96820-7df4-5ed3-a1d2-40358ae6c6d4" :answer/id #uuid "f7a96820-7df4-5ed3-a1d2-40358ae6c6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088932 :tutorial/content "Similar to transformations in a vector space, we can define a transformation between two *different* vector spaces. For instance, consider the transformation that maps the vector \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfrom $\\mathbb{R}^2$ to the vector \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ x-y \\\\ 2x+2y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nin $\\mathbb{R}^3,$ which can be written as\n\n![](images/ac/ac48dfb4fa4df769cc32789336d9f76960bde087351adf44328c33ebb1c40545.svg)\n\nThe *standard matrix* of this transformation is \n\n![](images/0a/0a94602cefa1750e0833e75a9a1e368d5d4164703fc85319db56cbfc28512194.svg)\n\nRecall that a transformation $\\mathbf{T}: V \\to W$ between two vector spaces $V$ and $W$ is *linear* if for any vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2\\in V$ and any scalar $k\\in\\mathbb{R}$, the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(k\\mathbf{v}_1) = k\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)$\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1+\\mathbf{v}_2) = \\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)+\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_2)$\n\nIt is easy to check that if a transformation can be represented as a matrix, then it is a linear transformation. Therefore, the transformation $\\mathbf{S}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nIn general, if $V$ and $W$ are $n$-dimensional and $m$-dimensional vector spaces respectively, then the standard matrix of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}\\!: V \\!\\rightarrow W$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix $T$." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087963 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
